      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "More than a third of women experience back pain during pregnancy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "The objective of the review was to assess the effects of preventive interventions and treatments for backache in pregnancy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SEARCH STRATEGY",
          "content": "We searched the Cochrane Pregnancy and Childbirth Group trials register and the Cochrane Controlled Trials Register."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SELECTION CRITERIA",
          "content": "Randomised trials of any treatment to reduce the incidence or severity of back pain in pregnancy, or to prevent back pain arising in pregnancy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DATA COLLECTION AND ANALYSIS",
          "content": "Trial quality was assessed and data were extracted independently by two reviewers."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "MAIN RESULTS",
          "content": "One trial of 109 women was included. This cross-over trial compared the use of a special shaped pillow to fit under the woman's abdomen (Ozzlo pillow) with a standard pillow. Women experienced less pain in the week when they used the Ozzlo pillow than in the week with the standard pillow (odds ratio 0.32, 95% confidence interval 0.18 to 0.58)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "REVIEWER'S CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Specially shaped pillows appear to help reduce back pain in late pregnancy and improve sleep."
        }
      ]},
